From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] wmadmoe, winegstreamer: The Windows Media Audio encoder (9403)

Wine had no WMA encoder (CLSID_CWMAEncMediaObject, WMADMOE.DLL): NAudio's
MediaFoundationEncoder.EncodeToWma, sink writers to .wma, WMContainer programs and DirectShow graphs
with the WMA encoder DMO found none. An MFT and a DMO as documented ("WMAudio Encoder", CBR): PCM or
float input set first, WMA 8 output types for it, one block per output sample; through wg_transform
(GStreamer's libav WMA v2 encoder), whose own block size and codec data go into the output type.
WMA 9 Pro/Voice/Lossless have no encoder here and are refused.
---
--- /dev/null
+++ b/dlls/winegstreamer/wma_encoder.c
@@ -0,0 +1,1181 @@
